This is a good metric to have and I like your approach to this (thank you for following up with code!), but I'm wondering if rarefaction may be an easier method to answering this question: https://grunwaldlab.github.io/poppr/articles/poppr_manual.html#producing-mlg-tables-and-graphs-bringing-something-to-the-table-

You could apply the filtering beforehand and use `rarecurve()` or `rareslope()` from the {vegan} package to assess how many MLGs are expected at a given sample size (though it does not extrapolate).

All the best,
Zhian

